From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] desktop-shell: do not fade out a closing surface without an
 output

With no output enabled (require-outputs=none and no display connected), a
mapped view has no output. When such a window closes and the close
animation is the default fade, desktop_surface_removed() dereferences
view->output to read its power state, and the compositor crashes with
SIGSEGV:

  desktop_surface_removed            desktop-shell/shell.c
  weston_desktop_xdg_toplevel_destroy libweston/desktop/xdg-shell.c
  weston_desktop_client_destroy      libweston/desktop/client.c
  wl_client_destroy

Skip the fade when the view has no output and destroy the surface
immediately, as is already done when the output is powered off.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-opus-5-5
---
 desktop-shell/shell.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/desktop-shell/shell.c b/desktop-shell/shell.c
--- a/desktop-shell/shell.c
+++ b/desktop-shell/shell.c
@@ -2018,6 +2018,7 @@
 	    shsurf->shell->win_close_animation_type == ANIMATION_FADE) {
 
 		if (shsurf->shell->compositor->state == WESTON_COMPOSITOR_ACTIVE &&
+		    shsurf->view->output &&
 		    shsurf->view->output->power_state == WESTON_OUTPUT_POWER_NORMAL) {
 			struct weston_coord_global pos;
 
